Here's the final program:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;
using System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata;

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    TypeInfoResolver = new DefaultJsonTypeInfoResolver()
};

// 1) Strongly-typed: GetTypeInfo(Type) → cast to JsonTypeInfo<T>
JsonTypeInfo<Person> personInfo = (JsonTypeInfo<Person>)options.GetTypeInfo(typeof(Person));

// 2) Probe without throwing: TryGetTypeInfo returns false if unavailable
bool found = options.TryGetTypeInfo(typeof(Person), out JsonTypeInfo? info);

// Example where it's NOT available (no resolver)
var emptyOptions = new JsonSerializerOptions { TypeInfoResolver = null };
bool found2 = emptyOptions.TryGetTypeInfo(typeof(Person), out _); // false

public record Person(string Name, int Age);
```

**Key APIs:**

| Goal | API |
|------|-----|
| Typed metadata | `options.GetTypeInfo(typeof(T))` → cast to `JsonTypeInfo<T>` |
| Probe without throwing | `options.TryGetTypeInfo(typeof(T), out JsonTypeInfo? info)` — returns `bool` |

`TryGetTypeInfo` (added in .NET 9) returns `false` instead of throwing when the type isn't resolvable — perfect for branching without try/catch.
